    "reasoning": "The variant is located within the APOE gene on chromosome 19 and is annotated on transcript ENST00000252486. It is described as substitution.\n\nThe submitted variant APOE:c.388T>C was evaluated using multiple publicly available genomic resources including Ensembl, ClinVar, HGVS validation and the educational ACMG-inspired evidence engine.\n\nThis interpretation is primarily supported by the ClinVar clinical significance of 'association'. The available record has a review status of 'no assertion criteria provided', providing additional confidence in the submitted interpretation.\n\nEnsembl predicts a missense variant. Missense substitutions alter a single amino acid but their biological impact depends on the affected residue and protein domain. Additional functional or computational evidence would normally be required.\n\nBased on the currently available evidence, this educational ACMG-inspired framework classifies the variant as Variant of Uncertain Significance.\n\nThe currently available evidence is insufficient to support either a pathogenic or benign interpretation. Additional population frequency data, computational prediction scores, functional assays and segregation studies would improve confidence in future analyses.\n\nThis report is intended exclusively for educational and research purposes and must not be used for clinical diagnosis or medical decision making.",
